{
  "about": ["Repositories whose own git settings start programs, and the fingerprint saw keeps for each: every", "setting of the repository's own scopes that `git_exec_keys.json` lists as running a program, every file", "under the hooks folder git runs hooks from when it is the repository's own, every file under the working", "tree's top folder holding that hooks folder, and the hook managers' own files (`git_hook_managers.json`),", "a pattern no file matches recorded as absent. saw's Python tests and the stand-in's Rust tests both read", "every case. `settings` is added to the repository's own settings, `files` are written under the case's", "folder, `operator_settings` is the operator's global settings, `@ROOT@` is the case's folder with every", "link resolved and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` its `config` folder. `expected` lists every entry but the absent ones,", "`starts_nothing` says whether the settings start no program, `digest` is the fingerprint's sha256, and", "writing `changed` must change it."],
